749 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 331 0 R
/E (Confirmation Bias: Seeking or interpreting evidence that supports existing beliefs \(e.g., a researcher focusing only on studies that confirm their hypothesis\). Availability Bias: Overestimating the likelihood of events that come to mind easily \(e.g., overestimating the danger of flying after hearing news of a crash\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
750 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 331 0 R
/E (Representativeness Bias: Judging probability based on how closely something resembles a stereotype or prototype \(e.g., assuming a quiet, bookish person must be a librarian rather than a salesperson\). Anchoring Bias: Over-relying on the first piece of information encountered when making decisions \(e.g., a clinician's initial diagnosis influencing all subsequent interpretation of symptoms\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
